# =====================================================================
# test_student.phon — Student-t regression validation.
#
# Status: DISABLED for the v1.0 frequentist suite. The reference
# produced by gen_reference_student.R is not trustworthy for any
# of the ten models (5 robust + 5 mild):
#
#   * Robust block — every model has converged = false. M2's speaker
#     SD is reported as ~574 (orders of magnitude wrong). M4's sigma
#     collapses to 2e-9. M5's slope SDs are < 1e-5 (boundary).
#   * Mild block — only M4 produces a finite logLik. M1 didn't
#     converge. M2/M3/M5 converged numerically but glmmTMB declined
#     to compute logLik.
#
# Comparing Phonometrica's Student-t engine against this reference
# would tell us nothing: a passing test would mean we're matching a
# broken fit, and a failing test would be ambiguous.
#
# The right way to validate Student-t (when we get to it) is against
# brms HMC, where the May 2026 fixes brought Phonometrica to within
# 0.17 brms-SD-units on every fit (project memory entry "Student-t
# Bayesian, May 2026 fixes"). That belongs in the Bayesian suite.
#
# This file is intentionally a no-op so run_all.phon can list it
# without producing failures or warnings. To re-enable when a clean
# frequentist reference is available: delete the early `return` and
# write per-block A.fit_and_check calls following the patterns in
# the other test_<family>.phon files.
# =====================================================================

let A = import("../lib/assert")
A.record_note("test_student.phon: SKIPPED — Student-t reference not reliable; see banner comment")
return null
